# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE IN BITUNG CITY

BITUNG CITY

NUMBER 8 OF 2019

MAYOR OF BITUNG

NORTH SULAWESI PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF BITUNG CITY

NUMBER 8 OF 2019

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE IN BITUNG CITY

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

MAYOR OF BITUNG,

Considering:







a. that the guarantee of respect, protection and fulfillment of Human Rights for every Indonesian Citizen in the Region is a duty that must be carried out by the Regional Government;
b. that Bitung City as a rapidly developing industrial city as one of the economic centers in North Sulawesi Province, has created many job opportunities so that many people from various areas outside Bitung City come to work within the Bitung City area and have the potential to create social friction which can result in the vulnerability of women and children to become victims of acts of violence;
c. that in the framework of implementing regional autonomy which refers to Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b and Article 236 of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, particularly in the field of women's empowerment and child protection which is included in concurrent government affairs that are the authority of Regional Government, namely mandatory government affairs not related to basic services, the Region establishes a Regional Regulation;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children from Acts of Violence in Bitung City;

In View of:







1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);
3. Law Number 7 of 1990 concerning the Establishment of the Second Level Regional Municipality of Bitung (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1990 Number 52, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3421);
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
5. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as has been amended several times most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
6. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Child Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 56);
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning the Empowerment of Child Victims of Violence;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
17. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 2036); as has been amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 120 of 2018 concerning the Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 157);

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BITUNG CITY

and

MAYOR OF BITUNG

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE IN BITUNG CITY.

