#### Article 20

Forms of community participation in preventing acts of violence against women and children, include:  
a. provision of safe houses and/or shelters;  
b. establishment and management of orphanages for children;  
c. establishment of child rehabilitation centers;  
d. active supervision of violence against women and children and reporting to the competent authorities; and  
e. providing assistance to victims.

#### Article 21

Families have the responsibility to prevent acts of violence against women and children, including:  
a. maintaining harmony in family relationships;  
b. providing assistance to victims;  
c. reporting every form of domestic violence to the competent authorities; and  
d. assisting the government in efforts to rehabilitate and reunify victims.

#### Article 22

Parents have the responsibility to prevent acts of violence against women and children, including:  
a. fostering love, affection and mutual respect in the family;  
b. providing assistance to victims; and  
c. reporting every form of domestic violence.

#### Article 23

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women is implemented through activities:a. formation of networks;  
b. implementation of coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns with the community, including the private sector and community organizations; and  
c. socialization of laws and regulations governing the protection of women.  
2. Prevention of acts of violence against children is implemented through activities:  
a. formation of networks;  
b. implementation of coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns with the community including the private sector and existing community organizations;  
c. socialization of laws and regulations governing the protection of children; and  
d. education to parents.  
3. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is implemented by involving:  
a. families;  
b. the community;  
c. the private sector;  
d. community organizations; and  
e. educational institutions.

#### Article 24

Provisions regarding the form and procedures for preventing acts of violence against women and children shall be further regulated in a Mayoral Regulation.

# CHAPTER V

IMPLEMENTATION OF SERVICES, ASSISTANCE AND RECOVERY FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN WHO ARE VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 25

1. Every woman and child who becomes a victim of acts of violence has the right to receive:   
a. protection;  
b. information;  
c. optimal services;  
d. continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;  
e. confidential handling;  
f. psychological and legal assistance; and  
g. guarantee of rights related to status as a family member or community member.  
2. The Regional Government guarantees the fulfillment of the rights of women and children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1).

#### Article 26

Children who are victims of acts of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 25, receive special rights as follows:  
a. the right to respect and full use for survival, growth and development;  
b. the right to basic services;  
c. the right to equal protection;  
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and  
e. the right to obtain freedom.

#### Article 27

1. Handling of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 25 is implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.  
2. Provisions regarding the form and procedures for handling children who are victims of acts of violence shall be further regulated in a Mayoral Regulation.

#### Article 28

1. Services for assistance and recovery of women and children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 25 are provided to women and children who are domiciled in the Region and who experience violence within the territory of the Region.  
2. Forms of assistance and recovery services as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented in the form of:  
a. women's empowerment;  
b. child rehabilitation;  
c. complaint, consultation and counseling services; and  
d. assistance services.  
3. Provisions regarding the form and procedures for assistance and recovery services for women and children who are victims of acts of violence shall be further regulated in a Mayoral Regulation.

# CHAPTER VI

## INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS

## Part One

Establishment of PPT

#### Article 29

Implementation of services for handling, assistance and recovery of women and children who are victims of acts of violence is carried out by the Regional Government by establishing PPT.

#### Article 30

1. Implementation of services for handling, assistance and recovery of women and children who are victims of acts of violence is carried out in an integrated manner by PPT.  
2. In addition to implementing services for handling, assistance and recovery of women and children who are victims of acts of violence, PPT takes preventive measures against acts of violence against women and children.  
3. PPT reports the implementation of services for handling, assistance and recovery of women and children who are victims of acts of violence as well as preventive measures against acts of violence against women and children to the Mayor through the Agency.

#### Article 31

PPT consists of elements:  
a. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of health;  
b. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of education;  
c. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of social affairs;  
d. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of trade;  
e. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of population;  
f. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection;  
g. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of community empowerment;  
h. regional apparatus that administers government affairs in the field of public peace and order;  
i. City Police Resort; and  
j. Non-Governmental Organizations.

## Part Two

PPT Counseling Division

#### Article 32

1. PPT has a counseling division in assistance and recovery services for women and children who are victims of acts of violence.  
2. The counseling division as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:  
a. legal division;  
b. health division;  
c. spiritual division; and  
d. psychology division.

## Part Three

Service Mechanism for Handling, Assistance and Recovery

#### Article 33

1. PPT may receive and send case referrals from or to other service units in a networked manner.  
2. PPT provides services and temporary protection in the form of Safe Houses.  
3. In the event that PPT does not yet have a Safe House, women and children who are victims of acts of violence are referred to PPT that has a Safe House.

#### Article 34

Forms of PPT services for women and children who are victims of acts of violence, include:  
a. medical services, in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of women and children who are victims of acts of violence carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;  
b. medical services for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;  
c. psychosocial services;  
d. legal services to assist women and children who are victims of acts of violence in undergoing legal processes; and  
e. economic independence services in the form of skills training and providing economic access so that women and children who are victims of acts of violence can be independent.
